Feature: Real-Time Heart Rate Telemetry Ingestion

  As a Clinical Trial Investigator
  I want wearable heart rate data normalized to UTC and deduplicated
  So that patient safety logs remain chronologically accurate and Part 11 compliant

  Background:
    Given the ClinSpark telemetry ingestion API is active
    And site "US-NY-101" is registered with timezone "America/New_York"

  Scenario Outline: Ingest duplicate telemetry payloads idempotently
    Given a wearable sensor transmits a heart rate reading with idempotency key "<idempotency_key>"
    And the raw payload contains local timestamp "<local_time>" with offset "<offset>"
    When the telemetry API receives the POST request payload
    Then the system should persist the reading in UTC as "<expected_utc>"
    And the HTTP response status code should be 200
    And sending the exact payload a second time should return HTTP 200 without creating a duplicate record

  Examples: Telemetry Deduplication and UTC Normalization Matrix
